collects basic information of the population such as gender and year and month of birth. Meanwhile,
households of one-seventh of the building units selected at random were required to answer the long-form
questionnaire, which collects detailed information such as ethnicity, nationality, place of previous residence,
education, employment and earnings.
As regards questionnaire content, questions about disability were removed from this round of Census to
reduce response burden, given that data on people with disabilities from the “System for Classification,
Registration and Certification of Disability” are fairly comprehensive. In view of population ageing, questions
on caregivers of individuals aged 60 and above with self-care disability were added to the Census.
